### Task Management API - request examples
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
# or JetBrains HTTP Client. Click "Send Request" above each block.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Health check (200 = app + database healthy, 503 = database down)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### List all tasks (newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks

### Create a task (only "title" is required)
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Set up CI pipeline",
  "description": "Build and test on every push with GitHub Actions",
  "priority": "HIGH"
}

### Get the task created above
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}

### Update a task (send only the fields to change)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
}

### Clear the description
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": null
}

### Delete a task (204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}

### --- Error examples ---

### 400 - validation errors (empty title, invalid enum, unknown field)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "priority": "URGENT",
  "unknownField": true
}

### 400 - malformed id
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/not-a-uuid

### 404 - task does not exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
